<title>UK: British Energy Feb sales up 15 pct.</title>
<headline>British Energy Feb sales up 15 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nuclear electricity producer British Energy Plc said on Tuesday that total sales reached 6.0 Terawatt hours (TWh) in February 1997, up from 5.22 TWh a year ago.</p>
<p>A Terawatt hour is the largest unit of measurement for electricity sales, representing one billion kilowatt hours.</p>
<p>The following table details sales from each power station in TWh:</p>
<p>				   1997			 1996</p>
<p>  Station		   Feb     Year	     Feb    Year</p>
<p>					  to date		   to date</p>
<p>  Hinkley Point B	 0.84    7.32	     0.81   9.13</p>
<p>  Hunterston B	    0.79    7.23	     0.80   7.92</p>
<p>  Dungeness B	     0.57    6.50	     0.22   1.97</p>
<p>  Heysham 1		 0.75    7.49	     0.41   5.84</p>
<p>  Hartlepool		0.69    8.19	     0.79   6.76</p>
<p>  Torness		   0.73    8.74	     0.75   8.13</p>
<p>  Heysham 2		 0.83    8.91	     0.62   8.79</p>
<p>  Sizewell B		0.80    7.56	     0.82   7.07</p>
<p>  Total		     6.00    61.94	    5.22   55.61</p>
<p>British Energy said total sales to customers in the year to date were 61.94 TWh, versus 55.61 TWh a year ago.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
